  "note": "This reanalysis isolates the token-axis ADDITIVITY STRUCTURE from the Gaussian-sensitivity SCALING that V2_E4 used and failed on (slope=0.35): P_damage_measured sums the MEASURED D_mse of matching F_S single-point configs at the same (block, r), rather than S_abs * eps_abs. Caveat: F_S singles always merge from the full 196-token input, while later schedule points merge fewer tokens -- the sequential-context diagnostic (26b) quantifies how much this shifts the per-point energy; P_damage_measured itself is unaffected since it is built from measured damages (D_mse), not those energies. Separately, a notebook audit found eps_abs is normalized by 197*384 in MergeScheduler (197 = 196 patch tokens + CLS) when the merge cost is only ever computed over the 196 patch tokens (CLS is never a merge candidate) -- the correct divisor is 196*384, so every eps_abs value reported anywhere in E4 is ~0.51% too small (197/196 = 1.00510...). This is flagged here for the camera-ready fix; it is IRRELEVANT to this reanalysis's verdict because P_damage_measured is built entirely from measured D_mse, never from eps_abs, and no re-sweep was performed to produce this file."
}